If I force it lowers to `ld/st` instead of `ldmatrix`/`stmatrix` like this:
```diff
diff --git a/lib/Tools/GenericSwizzling.cpp b/lib/Tools/GenericSwizzling.cpp
index 40ee9d775..68ce4dc24 100644
--- a/lib/Tools/GenericSwizzling.cpp
+++ b/lib/Tools/GenericSwizzling.cpp
@@ -646,7 +646,7 @@ optimalSwizzling(const LinearLayout &src, const LinearLayout &dst,
                      std::move(*maybeTileDst)});
   }

-  if (tiles.empty()) {
+  if (!tiles.empty()) {
     // We lower to an ld / st, but can't use LDS128/STS128
     auto smem = optimalSwizzlingLdSt(src, dst, bitwidth);
     return {smem, {0, 0}};
```

I got the perf back:
- Hacked version perf (apply the diff): 442 tflops
- baseline good version: 435 tflops
- baseline bad version: 359 tflops 

(All ran twice without tweaking gpu clocks on a 750W B200 machine)
